 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With gate and drain tied, the threshold at -250 μA is -0.6 to -1.4 V, typically -0.9 V. On-resistance has a guaranteed ceiling at three drive levels: 55 mΩ at -10 V, 68 mΩ at -4.5 V and 96 mΩ at -2.5 V. At -2.5 V it rises steeply with current, from about 90 mΩ near 1 A to about 175 mΩ at 10 A, while at -10 V it stays near 46 to 48 mΩ across 1 to 10 A (Fig.3). The gate is rated ±12 V and leaks no more than ±100 nA there."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Driving the gate to -10 V against -15 V on the drain at -1.0 A through 2.5 Ω, turn-on delay is 5.0 ns typ, rise 26 ns, turn-off delay 50 ns and fall 43 ns. Charging the gate to -4.5 V at -15 V and -4.4 A takes 22 nC typ, of which 3.0 nC is gate-source and 2.0 nC gate-drain. The gate charge curve holds a plateau near -2.3 to -2.5 V between about 2.7 and 5.5 nC (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The body diode carries up to -4.4 A continuously and drops no more than -1.2 V at -4.4 A with the gate at 0 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat and current",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 1.2 W dissipation and the 104 °C/W junction-to-ambient figure belong to a part soldered to a 1 in² pad of 2 oz copper on FR-4 in still 25 °C air. The continuous drain current holds about 4.4 A up to 25 °C ambient and falls to zero at 150 °C (Fig.8). Normalized on-resistance climbs from 1.0 at 25 °C to 1.5 at 150 °C (Fig.4). Junction and storage temperature both run from -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulsed current and safe operating area",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Pulsed drain current is -17 A, a repetitive rating bounded by the 150 °C junction limit at low enough frequency and duty that each pulse starts from 25 °C junction. The safe operating area at 25 °C ambient is bounded at low drain voltage by on-resistance and is cut off at 30 V drain voltage for each pulse length (Fig.7). Fig.9 gives the normalized transient thermal impedance for duty cycles 0.5, 0.3, 0.1, 0.05, 0.02 and 0.01 and a single pulse, all of them reaching about 1.0 to 1.17 at 1000 s."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A trench low-voltage power MOSFET in SOT-23. The molding compound carries a UL 94V-0 flammability rating and is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free; the leads are solder plated and meet the MIL-STD-750 method 2026 solderability test. Unit weight is 0.008 g."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Uses listed are battery protection, load switches and power management. Switching is high speed."
  }
 ],
